# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is git-ignored.
#
# This file configures **local development only** (`npm run dev`). Deployed
# builds do not read it:
#
#   ENQUIRY_TO, ENQUIRY_FROM   come from `vars` in wrangler.jsonc
#   RESEND_API_KEY             is an encrypted secret on each Worker
#   VITE_WHATSAPP_NUMBER       is a Build variable in the Cloudflare dashboard
#
# See the deploy section of README.md — putting a plain-text variable in the
# dashboard instead of wrangler.jsonc means the next deploy silently deletes it.
#
# Two namespaces here, and the difference matters:
#
#   VITE_*  is PUBLIC. Vite inlines it into the JavaScript the browser
#           downloads, so anyone can read it. Only ever put things here that are
#           already public.
#   others  are read by functions/api/enquiry.ts through the `env` binding and
#           stay on the server. Renaming a secret to VITE_ would publish it.


# ── Public: baked into the bundle ────────────────────────────────────────────

# WhatsApp number in international format. Non-digits are stripped, so
# "+91 93807 58632" and "91XXXXXXXX" both work. Missing = the page throws on
# load rather than shipping a dead link, so set it wherever the site is built.
VITE_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=91XXXXXXXX


# ── Server-only: never exposed to the browser ────────────────────────────────

# https://resend.com/api-keys — a bearer token for the whole Resend account.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxx

# Where enquiries land. Required: with this unset the endpoint returns 500
# rather than guessing. Must be a full address including the domain suffix.
#
# Until a domain is verified at https://resend.com/domains, Resend only delivers
# to the address the account was registered with — anything else comes back 403.
# So while sandboxed, this has to be that signup address, whatever it is.
ENQUIRY_TO=you@example.com

# The sender. onboarding@resend.dev is Resend's shared sandbox sender and is the
# only one that works before verification; the display name in front of it is
# free text, but the address itself is not. Putting an unverified address here —
# anything @nsmakeupartistry.com, before the domain is verified — is a 403 from
# Resend, which the handler surfaces as "could not be sent", not as a 500.
#
# Once send.nsmakeupartistry.com is verified, this becomes
# "Naga Sushmitha <enquiries@send.nsmakeupartistry.com>" — and remember to
# change it in wrangler.jsonc too, which is what deployed builds read.
ENQUIRY_FROM=Naga Sushmitha <onboarding@resend.dev>
